#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "aebe3048-cc5b-5340-a15e-d577ae2ee72a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5479" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n![](images/36/36c1ce5342657231cd78154ab4821a6a5bf9b78b74297ae5a4cdccdc2f6d5dcd.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/1c/1cab5be2ed7c560a3a5192473be4ff7b6cf6dc5728552f1d179c73affebefe20.svg)\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4\\cdot 3 & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092075 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/id #uuid "55e695b2-4581-5ba7-9604-506234b88323" :question/math-academy-id "e-5480" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n![](images/2c/2c669dd6f7c5fa368c5ea28961d2ef57cac9deaf7ba453f75a441b05206f6276.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/e4/e4e91261ec7f4a9a48847005a57730afa25f5e69a1f3818ad583acaadae639f8.svg)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation. \n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092076 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/id #uuid "a42d0af8-869c-5c2a-8182-22b14b9546e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5481" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](images/9f/9f13c3379e0613ce91669f6e52473dd11dc95360c422943764f30220dbccf430.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿![](images/03/039ee6073538580614cc07453132b811a4da81f438abf37197bb686057b4b66c.svg)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-3\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ 70-7\\lambda -10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-17\\lambda +52 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{(-17)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 52}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm 9}{2} \\\\  & =13,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "9e40836e-18e9-5df6-a930-05875b920335" :question/math-academy-id "e-5482" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](images/e3/e34b5bf690a1dd8f5275f2d742b264494386b95394bc7c32aaafb9eeba68e058.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/37/37f547d6ad345415a1cc2480adf227ec29e31a351cf935e584b9544e44347310.svg)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )-9\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2\\sqrt{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues $\\lambda={\\color{red}3}$ and $\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}.$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix ![](images/f4/f4e86a797cafe4857d5f135ec37d57e33368469767e50793f55b89ec7185c2eb.svg)\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d5cd195-916d-51d3-a145-ac3d8abbdf92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241427} {:answer/id #uuid "2bdfc526-d86a-5e73-baca-2112c1ad2358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +40=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241571} {:answer/id #uuid "35403cd9-ea2a-5b57-971f-4e9e59069317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -40=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241646} {:answer/id #uuid "a5cf22be-62ee-5bda-9228-41b20aca0652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242639} {:answer/id #uuid "dd32357c-ec00-5793-bb30-3f656df8bc88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d5cd195-916d-51d3-a145-ac3d8abbdf92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241427} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d00855c-44e0-5a49-b0df-a66417f8be4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "11ba9d38-2921-5184-bf8a-8d9ae2f12bf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-107987" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (8-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda )-6\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ -40-8\\lambda +5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2} & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ad3afc0-1147-5a90-b327-46c419abae45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =7$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402511} {:answer/id #uuid "bebf86c2-9d02-56e0-8de7-e3c093fdb99b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402512} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe3b5b3-5b53-5af3-a386-d1a9cac7570e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402513} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1b2964-fbf6-54e9-a3dc-5eb4004c5b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =7$ and $\\lambda =-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402514} {:answer/id #uuid "00de227b-1e08-5a35-a745-88b3e218426e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fe3b5b3-5b53-5af3-a386-d1a9cac7570e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402513} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c905a94-1e61-56fb-85f0-520ef6a3631a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fda33b2-0f78-5ef6-abce-da9e465c13f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-36780" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(P-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-1\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ 49-7\\lambda -7\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +54 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-14)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 54 \\\\  & =196-216 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $P$ does not have real eigenvalues."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a25f6950-9088-5ff9-8175-877d50a81da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426452} {:answer/id #uuid "a4036eef-ab8d-5137-83eb-70652e3c8c6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426453} {:answer/id #uuid "d1c7c087-5672-5851-ae11-572422abc236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426458} {:answer/id #uuid "d5281683-5678-50f6-a3d4-31872aa9352f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =-\\frac{5}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426460} {:answer/id #uuid "f7818e8c-878b-5236-95a6-67cb75479fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4036eef-ab8d-5137-83eb-70652e3c8c6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426453} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ff870f2-a00f-5d9f-a34a-712ea4371cad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95fd78c2-6907-5df8-b9fe-1452968ce01b" :question/math-academy-id "q-76362" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )(\\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ca2e399-f4d0-5ef7-8619-c99e58189fdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 8$ and $λ =-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091613} {:answer/id #uuid "b0d87e54-be80-520d-bd28-2382c0649bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-8$ and $λ = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091614} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e96c47-c916-5429-97af-08f89855dfcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 0$ and $λ =-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091615} {:answer/id #uuid "387e4d1f-ffff-549c-ae36-b18c3b2031ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091616} {:answer/id #uuid "752d5ced-51ff-5133-987b-6ddf5723816e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-5$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091617}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc34f16-51f9-5f2d-8f00-589e55c33860" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091612}] :question/id #uuid "4ecc70e1-e461-5246-9098-c27aa6c114e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-9341" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d755eb46-0df8-5f05-8ac3-9e4177f91e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 2$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091619} {:answer/id #uuid "0d80dad0-53c0-5d27-b5bd-04bb58893f9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091620} {:answer/id #uuid "509351d5-9c07-55db-9c5e-e06dc50201aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-2$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091621} {:answer/id #uuid "67a82505-4364-5ef4-ab13-711a8929a452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 4$ and $λ = 4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091622} {:answer/id #uuid "734d34a1-e1df-5119-85b5-09f5e2d2b9a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 1$ and $λ = 4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091623}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7fe56ff3-6e9f-5f5f-b666-d2ba2dce775a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091618}] :question/id #uuid "8d64c1c7-5e2c-5d9e-ad36-647b8fb50a8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-9346" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$."}]}
